\question{8}{10} The number of birds arriving at and leaving a park is recorded each day. The table shows the change in the total number of birds from last Monday to Friday. (An increase in the total number of birds by the end of a day is represented by a positive number.)

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|c|c|}
\hline
\textbf{Monday} & \textbf{Tuesday} & \textbf{Wednesday} & \textbf{Thursday} & \textbf{Friday} \\
\hline
$+34$ & $-26$ & $-12$ & $+51$ & $-42$ \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

\begin{subparts}
  \item Find the change in the number of birds from the beginning of Monday to the end of Friday.

  \item It is known that there were more than $40$ birds in the park at the end of Friday.
  \begin{subpartsii}[1]
    \item Find the least possible number of birds in the park before Monday.
    \item Candy claims that there must have been more than $35$ birds in the park before Monday. Do you agree? Explain your answer.
  \end{subpartsii}

  \item There were $50$ birds in the park at the end of Wednesday. Find the number of birds in the park by
  \begin{subpartsii}[1]
    \item the end of Friday,
    \item the end of Monday.
  \end{subpartsii}
\end{subparts}

